      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. I did it just in case we still have a backlight enable problem. But, just to warn everyone, you will see this backlight i2c error fail (everytime you open the lid). Because the EC and PCH enable signals are ANDed together. So, normally the EC gets the lid open and tries to write to the backlight controller, but this will fail because PCH enable is not asserted yet. Then when PCH comes up and enables backlight, it should successfully turn on backlight.\n\nSo, be warned if you see the i2c error for backlight, it\u0027s not necessarily a problem.",
